Changelog: 22-10-2026 19:31:16

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 22-10-2026 18:09:37

Added. Pictures from SteamGridDB for the games in Steam (owner, 22-10-2026), with core's covers. The app reads no
pictures from a game, so all four were always drawn from the app's icon and the game's title. With the suite's
SteamGridDB API key, entered under the new Covers… button (one key for every app of the suite, kept in
~/.config/bc250-bazzite-suite/steamgriddb-key), Update Game Mode first looks each ticked game up by its title, without
the tags of a file name ("Halo 3 (USA, Europe)" as "Halo 3"), and puts the cover, the wide picture, the banner and the
logo SteamGridDB has in place of the drawn ones; one it lacks stays drawn. The pictures are kept in
~/.local/share/bc250-xenia-manager/covers under the game's title ID (a disc image without one: a name from its title),
so a game is asked for once; a game in Steam not yet looked up turns Update Game Mode on. A refused key or no network
stops the lookup with a message and the shortcuts are written all the same. Without a key nothing changes. The artwork
is now drawn in the background job, after the lookup. install.sh --uninstall --purge removes the covers folder too; the installer test checks it. Test: the pictures in place of the drawn ones, the name they are
kept under, a file name's tags left out of the lookup, and Covers… with Update Game Mode in the window.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 14:25:29

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 13:23:31

Added. Xenia Manager: Xbox 360 games on the BC-250 with Xenia. Xenia has no stable releases, so the app pins one Xenia
Canary build, e6cd2e4 (20-10-2026), the Linux AppImage of its GitHub release, checked against its SHA-256, and says
when a build was published after it. The window says that Xenia's Linux build is experimental. It finds the games in
the chosen folders (Xbox 360 disc images, told by the disc's mark where Xenia looks for it; .xex files with their title
ID, an unpacked disc's default.xex under its folder's name; .zar archives; Games on Demand and Arcade packages under
the name in their header) and puts the ticked ones in Steam for Game Mode, "[X360] Title", the artwork drawn from the
app's icon. The Game Mode shortcuts run ~/.local/bin/bc250-xenia-run, which starts Xenia full screen
(--fullscreen=true); when Steam starts a game, a real controller is read instead of Steam's virtual one. Not tried on
the board yet: any game, the controllers under Steam Input.
